  "steps of 16 groups over a seed-permuted pool (3000 groups: 188 steps, last step 8 groups; 1500-group subsample: 94 steps, last step 12 groups); n_verify(step_groups, 0.25, step=t) as in E03 and L3i",
  "feat_vec = [agreement, n_distinct, mean_tokens, std_tokens, any_truncated, log_qlen] (6 dims), as in L3i and L3p",
  "greedy6u = allocators.GreedyOnlineAllocator unchanged (control): unscaled LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000), refit_every 20, prior_strength 2.0",
  "greedy6s = GreedyScaled, as in L3p: the cumulative verified set is refit as Pipeline(StandardScaler, LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)) on the same cadence; select() inherited, so the cold start before the first fit is the threshold order",
  "cell key is a constant 0 in every record and verified tuple; greedy selection never reads cells",
  "admitted = (errors - caught) / errors, with the errors of the run's own pool (main: 436; each subsample: its own count). No fixed-denominator variant: 436 is not a valid denominator for a half-pool",
  "permutation rng default_rng(1000+seed); selection rng default_rng(2000+seed) per run, as in L3p",
  "bootstrap: subsample of n // 2 = 1500 groups WITHOUT replacement per draw, rng default_rng(10000+b), B=200; threshold and greedy6s only, seeds 0-3, budget 0.25",
  "bias = mean of the B paired bootstrap diffs minus the seeds 0-3 full-pool point estimate; subsample SD = sample SD (ddof=1) of the B diffs",
  "percentile CI = 2.5 and 97.5 percentiles of the B diffs; basic CI = [2 * point - q97.5, 2 * point - q2.5]",
  "gold (proxy_error) used only for scoring and as the update label of verified groups",
  "gating: threshold reproduces E03 and the spec per seed; greedy6u reproduces runs/L3i and the spec per seed; greedy6s reproduces runs/L3p and the spec per seed; all checked before the bootstrap is read",
  "caveat: a half-pool subsample changes the loop itself (94 steps and 375 verified labels per run, versus 188 steps and 750 on the full pool), so the bias term can reflect learning-curve shrinkage as well as resampling. The threshold-only subsample mean is reported as a reference, because threshold fits no model"
